  "summary": "The Sedona Red Rock News editorial board commends the Sedona City Council for directing staff to shut down 11 Flock Safety ALPR cameras installed around the city beginning in June 2025. The editorial cites bipartisan public opposition, lack of prior public debate, concerns over ICE data-sharing, civil liberties, and 30-day data retention.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Five of the six council members present directed city staff to turn off the cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "from liberals who feared that the cameras would supply information to Immigration and Customs Enforcement, to conservatives who feared of the encroachments on their civil liberties",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "questioning why the camera data would be retained for 30 days, how it would be used, who would have access, how it might be sold or traded by Flock",
